<title>UK: TABLE - BARCLAYS H1 PROFITS UP EIGHT PCT.</title>
<headline>TABLE - BARCLAYS H1 PROFITS UP EIGHT PCT.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		59.2		   vs 55.3</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 13.5		   vs 11.5</p>
<p> Pretax pre-excepts     1,376*		 vs 1,270</p>
<p> Pretax		     1,271		  vs 1,270</p>
<p> Net interest income    2,037		  vs 1,949</p>
<p> Operating income	 3,866		  vs 3,775</p>
<p> Operating profit	 1,334		  vs 1,197</p>
<p> Debts provision	     90		  vs   148</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts had forecast pre-tax profits in a range between 1,216 and 1,347 million stg.</p>
<p>*Profits figure of 1,376 million stg is before one-off charges of 105 million stg following the UK government's recent budget.</p>
<p>Net interest income, operating income and operating profit are all before impact of budget.</p>
<p>Full company name - Barclays Plc.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4365</p>
</text>
